Input: {"question": "What was the profession of Henry Moseley?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0413-23a29397367b:d00", "start": 0, "end": 31, "text": "to know Albert, Prince Consort."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0413-23a29397367b:d00", "start": 32, "end": 220, "text": "In 1853 he was presented to a residential canonry in Bristol Cathedral; in 1854 he became vicar of Olveston in Gloucestershire, and was appointed chaplain in ordinary to the Queen in 1855."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0413-23a29397367b:d00", "start": 221, "end": 288, "text": "Moseley was elected a Fellow of the Royal Society in February 1839."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0413-23a29397367b:d00", "start": 289, "end": 457, "text": "He was also a corresponding member of the Institute of France, a member of the Council of Military Education, and vice-president of the Institution of Naval Architects."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0413-23a29397367b:d00", "start": 458, "end": 494, "text": "He died at Olveston 20 January 1872."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0413-23a29397367b:d00", "start": 495, "end": 593, "text": "While at Portsmouth Moseley wrote his first paper, \"On measuring the Depth of the Cavities seen on"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0413-23a29397367b:d01", "start": 0, "end": 31, "text": "to know Albert, Prince Consort."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0413-23a29397367b:d01", "start": 32, "end": 222, "text": "In 1853 he was presented to a residential canonry in Bristol Cathedral; in 1854 he became a marine biologist and was appointed a research fellow at the Marine Biological Association in 1855."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0413-23a29397367b:d01", "start": 223, "end": 290, "text": "Moseley was elected a Fellow of the Royal Society in February 1839."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2